{
  "id": "27884_korogeru",
  "headword": "転げる",
  "reading": "ころげる",
  "romaji": "korogeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to roll; to tumble; to roll over",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to roll; to tumble; to roll over",
      "explanation": "Of a person or object: to roll, tumble, or roll over, often suddenly or repeatedly. Frequently describes someone rolling around on the ground or floor."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27884_korogeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{坂道|さかみち}を{転|ころ}げ{落|お}ちた。",
      "english": "He tumbled down the slope.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27884_korogeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}たちは{芝生|しばふ}の{上|うえ}を{転|ころ}げ{回|まわ}った。",
      "english": "The children rolled around on the lawn.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27884_korogeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "あまりのおかしさに、おなかを{抱|かか}えて{転|ころ}げて{笑|わら}った。",
      "english": "It was so funny that we rolled around laughing, holding our sides.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). Nearly synonymous with {転|ころ}がる, but {転|ころ}げる more often appears in compound verbs and emphasizes a vigorous, tumbling motion.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {転|ころ}げ{落|お}ちる: to tumble down\n- {転|ころ}げ{回|まわ}る: to roll around\n- {転|ころ}げて{笑|わら}う: to roll around laughing\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {転|ころ}がる: to roll — the more common, neutral verb; {転|ころ}げる sounds livelier and is favored in the compounds above.",
